    "publishedAt": "2026-11-08",
    "summary": "Like any business, these two successes required months of design, development, and continuous refinement, along with faster and smarter decision-making, all enabled by technology from trusted partners like HPE. Setting a record as the youngest Formula One World Champion in history at 20 years old, Andrea Kimi Antonelli triumphed and won the 2026 FIA Formula One World Drivers’ Championship in only his second Formula One season. Among the new mandates was a hybrid power train with a 50:50 split between internal combustion engines and electric motor systems, requiring F1 engineering teams to completely redesign their cars. As data and analytics are key to producing the cars and, for drivers like Antonelli, learning how to maximize their performance, it made the Team’s HPE technology solutions and support—both in the factory and on the track—more critical than ever before.",
