    "summary": "With supply set to grow rapidly, substantial cuts to enterprise SSD orders from Chinese CSPs—coupled with a potential further contraction in consumer electronics demand—are expected to exacerbate oversupply. Strong demand for high-performance storage in North America continues to drive manufacturers to expand capacity and upgrade process technology. Additionally, brands seeking to control bill-of-materials (BOM) costs will need to reduce storage capacity specifications, resulting in a significant decline in average capacity per device and further widening the demand shortfall. Looking ahead to 2027, cuts to enterprise SSD demand from Chinese CSPs are expected to offset order growth in North America, while supply growth will significantly outpace demand throughout the year.",
