      "homepageEvent": null,
      "engineeringConclusion": "The GX Pro 8100 uses a Silicon Motion SM2508 PCIe 5.0 x4 controller found on other ‘budget’ high-end PCIe 5.0 drives. The SM2508 focuses a bit more on efficiency, keeping thermals well managed, but is still fast for a PCIe 5.0 drive. It also includes 2GB of DDR4-3200 cache for improved burst and sustained speeds. The storage chips are Kioxia BiCS8 218-layer TLC 3D CBA NAND, also found in the WD Black SN8100. Together, these reach speeds up to 14,900/14,000 MB/s (read/writes), nearly saturating PCIe 5.0 bandwidth. IOPS are listed up to 2.3/2.4M random r/w."
