    "publishedAt": "2026-11-27",
    "summary": "Samples are due March 2027, and Kioxia named its GP2 enterprise SSDs, rated for more than 18 million 512-byte random read IOPS, as its first product using it. The flash also reportedly has SLC endurance at 150,000 to 250,000 P/E cycles, at least 50x standard TLC, running at a 4.8 Gb/s interface speed. L SSDs for hyperscalers with up to 122.88TB capacity Micron's next-generation 3D NAND to double bit density with over 400 layers, offering extreme performance Kioxia Exceria Pro G2 2TB SSD Review — Speed built to last The GP2 Super High IOPS SSD will be Kioxia’s first product to use the new flash, promising high levels of performance, including up to 28 GB/s sequential reads, if it can saturate PCIe 6.0 x4 as expected. Exact specifications for the drive may differ, but what is clear is that later GP drives will target up to 100 million random-read IOPS that Kioxia and Nvidia have been working toward for AI servers.",
    "whyItMatters": "存储供给被 AI 数据中心吸走时，会同时影响服务器 BOM 和消费电子备货成本，需看缺货是否传导到客户排产。",
