    "publishedAt": "2026-11-27",
    "summary": "Billions of dollars are spent optimizing high-density server clusters, perfecting power distribution, and configuring complex cooling loops. Yet, an equally vital factor in facility efficiency sits entirely outside the server hall, and often out of mind: the building envelope. Using advanced fluid-applied, vapor-permeable Air and Water-Resistive Barriers (AWBs) can help to protect sensitive hardware from dangerous moisture levels, accelerate construction schedules, support compliance with building safety codes, and directly influence a site’s Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE). As developers race to deploy an estimated 100GW of new capacity globally by 2030 and effectively double the global infrastructure, the focus on building envelope integrity has never been more important.",
    "whyItMatters": "立讯需要把重点放在整机柜、供电、散热、高速线缆和连接器，而不是只看 GPU 或服务器品牌。",
