    "summary": "Telco’s footprint currently totals 9.1MW across six facilities Vodafone is set to expand its data center footprint in Kenya and Ethiopia, tripling the capacity of its Safaricom subsidiary. Vodafone said that it is planning to increase Safaricom’s data center capacity to 35MW across two ‘central data centers,’ though it hasn’t provided any further details on any planned projects or how the capacity might be split between the two countries. The telco is also set to be the landing partner for Meta’s upcoming Daraja cable in Mombasa, linking Kenya to Oman. iXAfrica's NBOX1 Nairobi Campus offers up to 22.5MW of capacity.",
