    "publishedAt": "2026-11-27",
    "summary": "Another cryptominer plans AI capacity UAE-based Bitcoin mining infrastructure company BitHash is targeting the AI colocation and hyperscale data center markets, with a proposed 250MW development in Oman among its plans. The company's UAE colocation page advertises rack densities of up to 270kW with direct-to-chip liquid cooling in Dubai and Abu Dhabi. It also markets private data center cages with power allocations ranging from 100kW to multiple megawatts. Elsewhere in Oman, DCD reported earlier this month that a consortium led by investment firm Mubbadrah plans a separate AI data center complex in Salalah with capacity of up to 400MW and an initial investment of $3 billion.",
