    "publishedAt": "2026-11-27",
    "summary": "Tied to Helios' up to 1GW solar project in Gua Musang, Malaysia German solar developer Helios Solar has signed a non-binding Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Malaysian data center developer Galaxy Venus Data Center (GDC) to explore supplying solar power to GDC’s proposed data center in Perak, Malaysia. Under the terms of the MoU, Helios has identified GDC as a prospective offtaker for its 1GW Helios Solar Park project in Gua Musang, Kelantan. The company announced last August that it was investing $2 billion in a computing cluster in Silicon Tech Park, a technology park west of Rayong, Thailand. Outside of the Gua Musang project, the company has an active development pipeline of around 380MW of solar capacity.",
